{
  "id": 487420926,
  "iid": 25016,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "epan: Try to raise the stack limit to 8MiB if needed, warn if it fails",
  "description": "Wireshark, TShark, and other related binaries are tested under the Linux\nand UN*X industry standard soft stack size limit of 8 MiB. On Windows,\nwhere the linker default stack limit is 1 MiB, the main thread maximum\n(reserve) stack size, which is set in the PE header of an executable[1],\nis set in CMake to 8 MiB as well.[2][3]\n\nIn POSIX environments where the current soft limit is less than 8 MiB,\nattempt to raise it to 8 MiB if the hard limit allows. If this fails,\nissue a warning noting that the configuration is untested and unsupported,\nand that segfaults and crashes due to stack exhaustion may occur.\nThere have recently been a large number of issues characterized by their\nreporters as security issues due to such stack exhaustion on crafted and\nfuzzed capture files in environments with 1 MiB or less of stack size.\nIndicate that these will not be treated as security issues as there is\nno warrant for proper operation under reduced stack size.\n\nThis is currently added only to libwireshark, but could be added to\nlibwiretap as well if necessary for programs such as capinfos or\neditcap that do not link with libwireshark. There are fewer file formats\nto address potential issues with than dissectors, however.\n\nPing #21074\n\n1 - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/debug/pe-format#optional-header-windows-specific-fields-image-only\n2 - Commit 086f4f1133e5b0b7a7172f5dff847d2bfc487461\n3 - Commit 48e66a5e24b8c8dd2fb683bf3521cde6d60c15c0\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
